Subject: [PATCH] pageset: ratelimit the command page exhaustion error

The command TX page pool shares its reserved pages with the beacon channel:
CMD_RSVED_PAGES_MAX is 2, and tx_page_get_for_channel() draws from the same
reserved_pages kfifo for both MORSE_SKB_CHAN_BEACON and MORSE_SKB_CHAN_COMMAND.
When the chip stops returning pages, the beacon tasklet drains that reserve once
per beacon interval and the command channel starves as well, so this error is
reported on every subsequent command attempt.

Observed on an AP with a 100 ms beacon interval: a few thousand identical lines
within four seconds. The console on this platform is a 115200 baud serial port,
and printk to a slow serial console is synchronous, so the flood burns CPU in
exactly the window where the health check work item and the pageset handler need
to run. That can turn a transient page shortage into a command timeout and a
firmware restart, which makes the flood self aggravating. It also buries the
first error, which is the one that explains the failure.

The beacon side of the same condition is already ratelimited
(MORSE_BEACON_ERR_RATELIMITED in beacon.c); only the command side is not.
MORSE_ERR_RATELIMITED takes the same arguments as MORSE_ERR, so this changes
only how often the message is emitted. The cmd_no_page statistic is still
incremented on every occurrence, so nothing is lost for diagnosis.

--- a/pageset.c
+++ b/pageset.c
@@ -325,7 +325,7 @@
 		MORSE_DBG(mors, "%s no page available for beacon\n", __func__);
 	} else if (channel == MORSE_SKB_CHAN_COMMAND) {
 		mors->debug.page_stats.cmd_no_page++;
-		MORSE_ERR(mors, "%s unexpected command page exhaustion\n", __func__);
+		MORSE_ERR_RATELIMITED(mors, "%s unexpected command page exhaustion\n", __func__);
 	}
 }
 
